From baab1ce1ddda660b5410aec1054a4073e19ff923 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:31:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Convert upstream's KEYS file
(https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/release/httpd/KEYS) with GnuPG into
KEYS.pgp, a plain OpenPGP keyring with every key GnuPG reads from it
(41); sqv cannot read the KEYS file itself: it holds 27 v3 (PGP 2) keys,
which Sequoia does not parse, so sqv rejects the whole file (GnuPG skips
such keys silently). Its Source line names the new file instead of
https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/release/httpd/KEYS, which is not what
the file holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 .gitignore |   1 -
 KEYS.pgp   | Bin 0 -> 310026 bytes
 httpd.spec |   7 +++++--
 sources    |   1 -
 4 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 KEYS.pgp

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index fdfbbf8..860a0b2 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -36,7 +36,6 @@ x86_64
 /httpd-2.4.41.tar.bz2.asc
 /apachectl.8
 /httpd-2.4.43.tar.bz2.asc
-/KEYS
 /httpd-2.4.46.tar.bz2.asc
 /httpd-2.4.48.tar.bz2.asc
 /httpd-2.4.49.tar.bz2.asc
diff --git a/KEYS.pgp b/KEYS.pgp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..999ee4f9fbf35943916622ccbaa18439ae5539fe
GIT binary patch
